        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Most people need one to two scoops of protein powder a day, about 25 to 50 g of protein. The right number is whatever closes the gap between your daily protein target and the protein your meals already supply, divided by the protein in one scoop of your powder.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Three scoops is fine for big, hard-training adults and unnecessary for most others. Keep powder to a minority of your total protein, choose a tested product if you use a lot of it, and talk to a doctor first if you have kidney disease or are pregnant.
          </p>
